  "finding": {
    "central_scale_coverage": "the current train distribution covers the real-dev p05 diameter of 6 px through the p90 diameter of 24 px",
    "remaining_scale_gap": "the current train distribution omits the real-dev 24 to 27 px p90-to-p95 tail and the 1 to 48 px full measured envelope",
    "failure_explanation": "scale coverage alone is insufficient to explain V23 real-dev recall 0.15568862275449102 because most of the measured central distribution is already inside the synthetic train range",
    "harness_defect": "the marker diagnostic used the minimum and maximum calibration-anchor coordinates as plot extents even though calibration anchors are not plot-boundary annotations",
    "harness_defect_evidence": "only 912 of 2004 truths lie inside the anchor rectangle and 1110 lie inside its 21-pixel expanded proposal search, matching raw-grid coverage of 1108 within grid quantization",
    "corrected_scope_result": "full-image grid and ink-supported recall are 1.0, but hard masks reduce recall to 0.8842315369261478 and the fixed classifier reduces it to 0.4555888223552894 while retaining 7653 false candidates",
    "patch_distribution_gap": "synthetic train contains no OCR-center hard-mask positives and only 1.19 percent artifact-center hard-mask positives, versus 3.74 percent and 16.57 percent on real-dev; its ink center lower tail is also much lighter",
    "generator_repair": "the corrected synthetic generator now spans the measured diameter, rendered footprint, ink, OCR-center mask, artifact axis-crossing mask, and prohibited-structure ranges with disjoint train and dev seeds",
    "feasibility_result": "mask-preserving proposal coverage is complete, but the frozen V21 classifier fails the corrected synthetic dev gate and hits one prohibited structure per scene",
    "candidate_result": "V24 P1 clears every corrected synthetic dev gate at the fixed 0.25 threshold after one void pre-sealed dtype attempt and one valid training run",
    "real_dev_contradiction": "V24 real-dev fails at precision 0.12265 and recall 0.57036 despite complete proposal and mask-preserved coverage, with 17867 false candidates above the fixed classifier threshold",
    "negative_generator_gap": "synthetic negatives omit the real faint tail because ink-maximum p05 is 0.83375 versus real 0.19216, and omit OCR-heavy negatives because OCR-mask mean p95 is 0.02296 versus real 0.72727",
    "negative_generator_repair": "faint-line and OCR-heavy negative families now cover both measured real envelopes without changing truth counts, truth mask hits, positive distribution gates, dtype, or split isolation",
    "retry1_diagnosis": "every final false positive came from generic negatives, so quantile-grounded retry2 restored 21681 generic samples while preserving measured tail coverage",
    "retry2_result": "the same unconsumed P1 now clears every fixed synthetic dev gate at threshold 0.25",
    "retry2_runtime": "candidate-only C# binding, mask preservation, multiradius geometry, fixed threshold, CPU execution, and fail-closed production behavior all pass focused verification",
    "retry2_real_dev_contradiction": "retry2 improves real-dev recall to 0.59980 but precision remains 0.12034 with 21274 false candidates above threshold, so scalar negative coverage and sampling were insufficient",
    "required_next_diagnosis": "measure aggregate spatial morphology of retry2 above-threshold false proposals on synthetic dev and real-dev, repair synthetic topology, and re-pass synthetic gates before another model or private run"
